						  &lt;div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-block paragraph--view-mode--default"&gt;
          
            &lt;div class="field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Scope&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;IDRC has helped graduate students undertake research in the field of international development since 1982. The Bene fellowship, a bequest from the estate of John G. Bene, is offered to Canadians and permanent residents of Canada pursuing master’s or doctoral studies at a Canadian university. Candidates should have an academic background that combines an interest in forests (landscape and forest management and restoration, forestry, agroforestry), environment, ecology and food systems, with a social sciences lens (gender and inclusion, Indigenous knowledge and science, biodiversity conservation, governance of nature).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;This fellowship aims to facilitate practical field research on gender-responsive integrated forest, landscape and food systems restoration and management including within fire prone, degraded or disputed landscapes. Linking the broader climate-food-inclusivity nexus, it emphasizes nature-based solutions and approaches that have the potential to drive transformative change for smallholder farmers, including youth, women, and Indigenous communities in developing countries. The successful candidate will propose research that benefits less privileged people in developing countries aiming to increase the resilience of individuals and forest/agroforest communities facing difficult contexts and challenges. Note that work focused on genomics and/or genetic modification is not eligible.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;Proposals that align with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://idrc-crdi.ca/en/initiative/post-fire-forest-and-landscape-restoration-revive" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;IDRC's REVIVE Initiative on post-fires forest and food restauration and food systems transformation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt; are welcome.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang="EN"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang="EN"&gt;Learn more about &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.idrc.ca/en/bequest-bene-family" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"&gt;&lt;span lang="EN"&gt;John G. Bene.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Eligibility&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-CA"&gt;This call is open to Canadians and permanent residents of Canada pursuing master’s or doctoral studies at a Canadian university. The award under this call will cover costs of field research conducted for a master’s thesis or doctoral dissertation in one or more countries of the Global South. Please consult the detailed call document for more specific eligibility requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;More details&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;For more information, please read the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://idrc-crdi.ca/en/idrc-invites-applications-john-g-bene-fellowship-2026"&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;detailed call for proposals document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://idrc-crdi.ca/en/frequently-asked-questions-john-g-bene-fellowship-2026-strengthening-inclusive-community-led-nature"&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;frequently asked questions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      
